\f0\b\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf2 Phase 3: Computational Journalism and Data Extraction
\f1\b0\fs32 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf2 This phase represents an escalation in technical rigor. Students are introduced to the Python programming language through pair-programming exercises. Students write scripts utilizing libraries like BeautifulSoup to scrape unstructured web data and Pandas to clean chaotic datasets. Emphasis is placed on data ethics, the garbage in, garbage out paradigm, and secure virtual environments. 
\f1\fs32 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf2 Fulfills the SLO requiring students to utilize coding for deep research. Prepares students for the sheer scale of data analysis required in the Summative Capstone Investigation, ensuring they are not limited by manual search capacities. 
