\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \'a0
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b Technological Integration: The Custom Gemini Gem
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 A unique learning experience integrated directly into the instructional sequence of the course is the deployment of a custom Gemini Gem. This specialized artificial intelligence operates as an interactive, continuously available teaching assistant for students navigating the complexities of digital forensics. Crucially, the Gem is explicitly programmed and constrained to guide students through the verification process without ever completing the cognitive labor for them, thereby avoiding the pitfalls of activity-oriented design that lacks a minds-on component.
\f1 \

\f2 The architecture of the Custom Gemini Gem is mapped to Bloom\'92s Taxonomy to provide scaffolded, differentiated instructional support:
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2 \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}At the 
\f0\b Understanding
\f2\b0  level, the Gem is programmed to act as a conversational tutor, capable of breaking down highly complex technical concepts into accessible plain language.
\f1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}At the 
\f0\b Applying
\f2\b0  level, the Gem serves as a pair-programming assistant for computational journalism. It is instructed to prompt students to identify their own syntax errors, explaining the logical flow of data extraction libraries to ensure students understand 
\f3\i how
\f2\i0  the code functions.
\f1 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}At the 
\f0\b Analyzing
\f2\b0  level, when a student is presented with a suspicious piece of digital media, the Gem guides them through a step-by-step verification checklist. It acts as an analytical sounding board, prompting the student to cross-reference historical weather data via Wolfram Alpha, verify Google Analytics IDs in the source code, and actively triangulate their findings before reaching a premature conclusion.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 By interacting with this custom Gem throughout the semester, students experience a controlled, educational interaction with generative AI. This instructional strategy achieves the dual goal of actively demystifying the technology while simultaneously teaching students how to critique its outputs and biases.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Lesson Plan Blueprint: Visual Verification and Digital Forensics
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b General Course Context and Established Goals
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Topic Focus:
\f2\b0  Visual Verification, Image Provenance, Spatial Mapping, and Media Deconstruction.
\f1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Estimated Student Time on Task:
\f2\b0  Two Weeks (approximately 12-14 hours of total student engagement, encompassing synchronous live sessions, rigorous readings, and applied performance tasks).
\f1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Course-level SLO Addressed:
\f2\b0  Deconstruct complex digital media to detect fabrication, temporal shifts, and context shifts, while utilizing specialized digital forensic tools to establish provenance.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Enduring Understandings and Essential Questions
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Enduring Understanding:
\f2\b0  Visual media in the modern digital ecosystem can no longer be assumed to be authentic or human-generated. Trust in digital imagery requires the interrogation of source and metadata. Furthermore, students must understand how \'93False Context\'94 (the recycling of genuine imagery to fit a false breaking news narrative) is weaponized to hijack human emotion and bypass cognitive skepticism.
\f1 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Essential Questions:
\f2\b0  How does visual fakery persuade audiences where fabricated text fails? Why does the human brain inherently struggle to recognize manipulated content when viewing high-emotion imagery during crises? Does the absence of an algorithmic digital watermark inherently prove that an image is authentic? 
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Week 1: Provenance, Metadata, and the Limits of Detection
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Overview:
\f2\b0  During the first week of this module, students will be introduced to the foundational concepts of reverse image searching, the forensic analysis of metadata, and the ongoing adversarial arms race between synthetic media generation models and AI detection systems.
\f1 \
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Guided Readings and Resources:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl1
\f3\i \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Bellingcat: A Beginner's Guide to Social Media Verification
\f2\i0 .
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl1
\f2 \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Specific modules from the Bellingcat Online Investigations Toolkit focusing on image verification protocols.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl1
\f3\i \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}The Indicator Guide to AI Labels
\f2\i0  and the technical documentation for Google DeepMind\'92s SynthID.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Guided Reading Questions for Students:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl1
\f2 \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}What are the strict limitations of relying on EXIF data when investigating images scraped from major social media platforms like Meta or X? 
\f1 \
\ls6\ilvl1
\f2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}How do Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) actively learn to correct visual flaws, and why is human visual inspection increasingly insufficient for deepfake detection? 
\f1 \
\ls6\ilvl1
\f2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Explain the methodology of frequency domain embedding utilized by provenance tools like SynthID. How does this technique survive extreme digital compression? 
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Live Session Agenda (Synchronous):
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl1
\f2 \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Lecture exploring the psychology of visual misinformation, detailing the specific differences between False Context and fully Manipulated Content.
\f1 \
\ls6\ilvl1
\f2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Interactive, instructor-led demonstration of the RevEye browser extension, TinEye, and Yandex, teaching students how to locate the absolute earliest instance of a digital image on the internet.
\f1 \
\ls6\ilvl1
\f2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Live laboratory analysis of EXIF data utilizing tools like FotoForensics or Jeffrey\'92s Image Metadata Viewer, teaching students to extract camera settings, modification timestamps, and hidden GPS coordinates.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Discussion Topic (Asynchronous):
\f2\b0  Based on the critical essay 
\f3\i Your AI Use Is Breaking My Brain
\f2\i0 , students will debate the ethical responsibilities of massive social media platforms regarding the automatic watermarking or algorithmic throttling of synthetic media. Students are required to post an initial analytical reflection and respond comprehensively to at least two peers, explicitly identifying points of technical or philosophical disagreement.
\f1 \
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Formative Assessment Task:
\f2\b0  Students will complete a specialized interactive module utilizing the custom Gemini Gem. They will be presented with three highly viral, suspicious images. They must prompt the Gem to assist them in verifying the source of the images, subsequently submitting their complete chat transcript alongside a brief methodological analysis evaluating the Gem's effectiveness and identifying any hallucination encountered during the process. This directly serves as acceptable evidence of their prompting logic and analytical oversight.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Week 2: Video Forensics, Geolocation, and Authentic Application
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Overview:
\f2\b0  Building directly upon the static image verification competencies acquired in Week 1, students transition to the far more complex interrogation of video content and the precise art of mapping transient digital assets to verifiable, real-world geography.
\f1 \
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Live Session Agenda:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl1
\f2 \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Detailed demonstration of the InVID browser extension, teaching students how to fragment rapidly moving video files into static keyframes and run deep forensic filters to detect digital cloning or tampering.
\f1 \
\ls7\ilvl1
\f2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Workshop on manual geolocation and chronolocation methodologies. Instructor will guide students in cross-referencing shadow lengths, historical weather conditions, obscure street signs, and architectural details visible in a video against high-resolution satellite imagery on Google Earth, Google Street View, and crowdsourced mapping platforms like Wikimapia.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Summative Assessment (Video Verification Exercise):
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl1
\f3\i \cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Task Description:
\f2\i0  Students will be provided with a brief, contentious video clip currently circulating on a closed platform like Telegram or a viral network like TikTok, purportedly showing a recent kinetic military action or political protest.
\f1 \
\ls7\ilvl1
\f3\i {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Performance Requirement:
\f2\i0  Students must deconstruct the video utilizing all acquired competencies. They must fragment the frames via InVID, establish provenance to prove if the footage has been recycled from a past conflict (identifying False Context), utilize advanced satellite mapping to geolocate the exact physical intersection where the video was filmed, and analyze historical meteorological data to definitively corroborate the timestamp.
\f1 \
\ls7\ilvl1
\f3\i {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Acceptable Evidence:
\f2\i0  Students must submit a formal, structured verification report. Crucially, the report must avoid declarative certainty unless supported by triangulated proof, strictly adhering to the discipline of verification. The grading rubric will heavily weight the transparency of the student's methodology and the clear articulation of the steps taken to reach their conclusion, aligning perfectly with the AI-resilient frameworks established in Stage 2 of the course design.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \'a0
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b Conclusion
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 The pedagogical framework outlined in this course development plan applys the Understanding by Design methodology to the rapidly evolving challenges of modern media education. The JOUR 3318 curriculum empowers students to combat global disinformation, anchoring the instruction in philosophical questions regarding the nature of truth, honesty, and AI authorship in efforts to move beyond traditional, software-specific technical training.
\f1 \

\f2 The deployment of authentic performance tasks and AI-resilient assessment rubrics ensures that students are evaluated not on their passive ability to aggregate facts, but on their mastery of the investigative process and their capacity for rigorous critical thought in an era dominated by artificial media. In addition, through a carefully sequenced integration of open-source intelligence methodologies, Python-driven computational research, and advanced machine learning platforms, students are equipped with a level of professional, highly transferable competencies.
\f1 \

\f2 Ultimately, this integrated instructional design ensures that students who complete the "Digital Investigative Techniques" course do not merely learn to survive within a polluted digital landscape. Instead, they gain the analytical frameworks, the technical firepower, and the enduring ethical conviction necessary to actively investigate and clean that environment. By transforming from passive consumers into adaptable creators, these students are prepared to fulfill the fundamental democratic imperative of journalism: providing the public with the verified, contextualized information required to create a more just, honest, and informed world.
\f1 \

\f2 \'a0
